  "worked_solution": "Solving our equation for $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n3y={z}^{2}-9{x}^{2}\\,\u27f9\\,y=\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}-3{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,z) & =\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8x,\\,\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}-3{x}^{2},\\,z\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is $\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}-3{x}^{2}.$",
